        <div class="card-body">
            <h2>Remove Background While Keeping the Same Resolution – Browser‑Based AI Tool</h2>
            <p>
                Many online background removers downsample or resize your image, resulting in blurry or low‑quality output. 
                Our tool is different: it <strong>preserves the exact original resolution</strong> of your image. 
                Whether you upload a 400×400 product photo or a 4000×3000 high‑res image, the output PNG will have the same width and height.
            </p>
            <p>
                This is essential for e‑commerce product photos, graphic design assets, and any professional use case where quality and precise dimensions matter.
            </p>

            <h3>Why Our Browser‑Based Background Remover is Unique</h3>
            <ul>
                <li>✔ <strong>Same resolution output</strong> – no resizing, no cropping, no quality loss.</li>
                <li>✔ <strong>100% client‑side</strong> – your images never leave your device. No upload, no server, complete privacy.</li>
                <li>✔ <strong>AI‑powered</strong> – uses U²‑Net deep learning model running locally via WebAssembly.</li>
                <li>✔ <strong>Works offline after first use</strong> – the AI model is cached in your browser.</li>
                <li>✔ <strong>No signup, no watermark, completely free</strong>.</li>
            </ul>

            <h3>How to Remove Background and Keep Resolution</h3>
            <ol>
                <li>Click or drag & drop an image (JPG, PNG, WEBP, BMP).</li>
                <li>The AI model loads once (first time ~40MB download).</li>
                <li>Click “Remove Background” – processing happens locally.</li>
                <li>Preview the result with transparent background, same dimensions.</li>
                <li>Download the PNG – resolution is preserved exactly.</li>
            </ol>

            <h3>Technical Explanation: How Resolution is Preserved</h3>
            <p>
                The AI model generates a segmentation mask at full resolution. It then applies that mask to your original image data 
                without any scaling or interpolation. The output PNG is constructed using the original pixel dimensions, 
                ensuring that every detail remains sharp and intact.
            </p>

            <h3>Use Cases Requiring Exact Resolution</h3>
            <ul>
                <li><strong>E‑commerce product images:</strong> Platforms often require specific dimensions (e.g., 1000×1000).</li>
                <li><strong>Print materials:</strong> High‑resolution images must not be downsampled.</li>
                <li><strong>Web design:</strong> Maintain retina/HD quality.</li>
                <li><strong>Archival / medical imaging:</strong> Pixel‑perfect preservation.</li>
            </ul>

            <p>Our tool is built with privacy first: all processing happens inside your browser. No image ever leaves your computer.</p>
        </div>
    </div>
</div>

